vismod invokes the external FFmpeg and FFprobe binaries at runtime for
video frame extraction. FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard and is
licensed separately (LGPL/GPL depending on build); vismod does not bundle
or link FFmpeg — the Docker image installs it from the distribution's
package repository.

Third-party Go modules are used under their respective licenses (see
go.mod); notable direct dependencies: spf13/cobra, spf13/viper,
prometheus/client_golang, cloud.google.com/go/vision, redis/go-redis,
golang.org/x/sync (all Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, or MIT).
